<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Our Indigenous Heritage – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Indigenous Heritage</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Researching Our History</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write simple texts giving key information about oneself and one's culture. Interactive: Edit narrative texts written by peers.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a simple text sharing a personal cultural tradition (e.g., "Describe your family's celebration of Carnival and explain a key tradition, such as attending parades or dancing at the culcos."). Can edit a peer's narrative on Indigenous traditions by suggesting additional details (e.g., "I think you can add more details about the colors in traditional clothing."). Can edit a peer's descriptive paragraph on a festival (e.g., "You could add some adjectives like 'colorful' or 'exciting' to make it sound more vivid and fun.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 34%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b><br>(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays images of different Panamanian Indigenous clothing patterns (e.g., Guna molas, Ngäbe-Buglé chakaras). Students brainstorm adjectives they can use to describe them (e.g., <i>vibrant, colorful, traditional, intricate, handmade</i>). Teacher writes suitable adjectives on the board. This activates vocabulary from previous lessons and sets the stage for descriptive writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models writing a simple descriptive sentence about one of the patterns, e.g., "The Guna molas have <b>vibrant</b> and <b>colorful</b> patterns that represent their <b>ancestral</b> traditions." The teacher explicitly shows how adjectives add detail and how to use the present simple for descriptions. Teacher also models pronunciation, focusing on stress in "<b>vibrant</b>" and "<b>ancestral</b>."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Are 'vibrant' and 'colorful' verbs or adjectives?" (Adjectives)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do these adjectives tell us more about the patterns, or about actions?" (More about the patterns)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b><br>(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short narrative excerpt (1-2 paragraphs) describing an aspect of Indigenous culture in Panama, focusing on its history and preservation. The text includes examples of present simple, past simple, present perfect, and descriptive adjectives.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Example Text:</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; font-style: italic;">"Panama is home to <b>diverse Indigenous cultures</b>, each with <b>unique traditions</b>. The Guna people, for instance, <b>have preserved</b> their language and <b>vibrant</b> art forms like molas for centuries. Historically, some groups, like the Emberá, <b>migrated</b> from Colombia in earlier times. Today, their communities continue to <b>honor ancestral customs</b>. This rich <b>heritage</b> is a <b>valuable</b> part of our nation's <b>history</b>, and it's essential that we all <b>respect</b> and <b>protect</b> it."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students will be able to interpret and understand short descriptive texts about cultural heritage.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Gist question: "What is the main topic of this text?" (Panama's Indigenous cultures and their preservation).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Matching: Match underlined vocabulary words (e.g., <i>diverse, vibrant, heritage, preserve</i>) from the text to their definitions on the board.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Sentence completion: "The Guna people _______ their language and art." (have preserved).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b><br>(Accuracy focus on Writing)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice using present simple, past simple, present perfect, and descriptive adjectives (<i>vibrant, colorful, preserved, traditional, diverse, ancestral, cultural, historical</i>) to describe Indigenous cultures.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice (Cloze Activity):</b> Students receive a worksheet with sentences about Indigenous groups. They fill in the blanks using a word bank of target vocabulary and correct verb tenses. E.g., "The Emberá people _____ (preserve) their <b>cultural</b> background." "Their _____ (traditions) are very ____ (historical)."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled (Sentence Expansion):</b> Students are given simple sentences about Indigenous groups (e.g., "The Wounaan make baskets.") and a list of adjectives/adverbs. They rewrite the sentences, adding detail and using appropriate grammar. E.g., "The Wounaan people <b>skillfully</b> make <b>beautiful, traditional</b> baskets." This enhances descriptive writing.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaborative Sentence Building:</b> In pairs, students receive three prompts (e.g., "Talk about Guna language," "Describe a Ngäbe-Buglé ceremony," "Mention Emberá history"). For each prompt, they must collaboratively write one complex sentence (using at least one adjective, one target noun, and one verb in either present simple, past simple, or present perfect). They must also focus on stress in multisyllabic words as they discuss their sentences (e.g., "<b>Indigenous</b>," "<b>migration</b>").</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b><br>(Communicative task where students USE the language)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual descriptive paragraph writing followed by peer editing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students are tasked with writing a descriptive paragraph (6-8 sentences) about a personal cultural tradition or an Indigenous tradition in Panama. They must include:</li>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least one sentence using present simple, one using past simple, and one using present perfect.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least five target vocabulary words (nouns: <i>traditions, heritage, customs, community</i>; verbs: <i>preserve, celebrate, honor</i>; adjectives: <i>vibrant, colorful, traditional</i>).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Phrases for acknowledging cultural value (e.g., "The Guna people's customs are unique and valuable to our nation.") or sharing historical importance (e.g., "Groups like the Emberá have lived here for centuries and maintain traditional ways.").</li>
                    </ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Once paragraphs are complete, students exchange them with a peer. Each student edits their peer's paragraph, focusing on:</li>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Suggesting additional descriptive adjectives or details to make the text more vivid (e.g., "You could add some adjectives like 'colorful' or 'exciting' to make it sound more vivid and fun." or "I think you can add more details about the colors in traditional clothing.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Checking for correct use of target vocabulary and grammar structures.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Providing constructive feedback on clarity and organization.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students then receive their edited paragraphs back and make revisions.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b><br>(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation of peer editing and review of final revised paragraphs using a simple rubric.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their revised descriptive paragraph about a cultural tradition.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of target vocabulary (at least 5 words).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct application of present simple, past simple, and present perfect.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Inclusion of descriptive adjectives to add detail.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and coherence of the written text.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effective suggestions during peer editing.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new adjective you used today to make your writing more descriptive?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing you learned from editing your peer's paragraph?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How has practicing writing about our Indigenous heritage helped you understand its importance?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What challenges did you face when writing about the traditions, and how did you overcome them?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What specific writing aspects (e.g., use of adjectives, verb tenses, paragraph structure) worked well, and where do students still need more support?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How engaged were students in the peer editing process? Did they provide useful feedback?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What adjustments or additional scaffolds might be needed for students to confidently write more complex texts about cultural topics?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration), students will use the writing skills developed today to summarize information about Indigenous cultures and present their findings in a 21st Century Skills Project.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>